<?xml version='1.0' standalone='yes'?>
<!DOCTYPE PLUGIN [
<!ENTITY name      "shive">
<!ENTITY author    "heinrichchristopher">
<!ENTITY version   "2026.09.24">
<!ENTITY launch    "Settings/Shive">
<!ENTITY gitURL    "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/heinrichchristopher/shive/main">
<!ENTITY pluginURL "&gitURL;/shive.plg">
<!ENTITY pkgURL    "https://github.com/heinrichchristopher/shive/releases/download/&version;">
<!ENTITY pkgName   "shive-&version;-noarch-1.txz">
<!ENTITY pkgMD5    "99811fad030a44af29c2d29a00068be9">
<!ENTITY plgPath   "/boot/config/plugins/&name;">
<!ENTITY emhttp    "/usr/local/emhttp/plugins/&name;">
]>

<PLUGIN name="&name;" author="&author;" version="&version;" launch="&launch;"
        pluginURL="&pluginURL;" min="7.2.0" icon="shive.png"
        support="https://github.com/heinrichchristopher/shive/issues">

<CHANGES>
###2026.09.24
- Excluding a child dataset from the snapshot now also excludes its container from stop/resume
  (also in the editor's "Show linked containers" preview). Exclusion checklists show a red minus.
- Fix: a check pattern (grep -q in a pipeline) could report "not found" on a match. Worst case the
  orphan sweep deleted a valid child snapshot. All occurrences fixed.
- Fix: a container that started on the second attempt still raised "containers still DOWN".
- Fix: rollback restore claimed a safety snapshot that the rollback itself destroyed.
- Fix: disaster-recovery restores came back read-only.
- Backup runs and dataset restores no longer run at the same time.
- Delete refuses the newest snapshot on a backup target (the base of the next backup).
- Two schedules writing into the same target dataset are rejected at save time.
- Settings are validated server-side; log access and cleanup only touch Shive's own folders.
- Clearer recovery messages (which host, zfs receive -A for a stuck transfer); dry-run shows
  everything a real run would delete and creates nothing.
###2026.09.21
- Replication base lost on the target (a snapshot deleted or created there by hand): detected by
  GUID before sending, explained in plain terms with the concrete recovery step, and shown in the
  notification and History tab instead of a raw "does not match incremental source" error.
- Fix: a new snapshot reusing the name of an older one still on the target was taken for "already
  sent" - Shive reported success without sending. Now verified by GUID.
###2026.09.15
- Fix: dry-run of a schedule with a target-level exclusion showed nothing under SEND_LOCAL/
  SEND_REMOTE - the check deciding what to send relied on a real snapshot that dry-run never
  creates. Dry-run now correctly shows what would be sent and what would be excluded.
- Fix: pruning a target whose dataset has never been created yet (first-ever run, dry-run, or a
  skipped/failed send) crashed with "FATAL: retention classification failed" instead of reporting
  "nothing to prune yet".
###2026.09.14 (.1/.2: GUI fix + re-release after a mistagged .1)
- Dataset exclusions: recursive schedules can leave individual child datasets out of the snapshot
  entirely, or out of just one replication target (additive to the snapshot-level exclusion).
- GUI: the per-target exclusion lists now only offer datasets that still get a snapshot.
###2026.09.12
- Run logs and retired run-state files are now capped (newest 200 / 50) instead of growing for
  the whole uptime; the cron file is no longer rewritten to flash when it is already correct.
- The snapshot tag prefix is derived in one place (PHP) and read by all three scripts, instead of
  being rebuilt from a literal in two of them.
###2026.09.11 (cleanup)
- Validation: backup target roots, remote host/user/port are now checked the same way source
  datasets always were, at save time instead of failing later at run time.
- Removed dead code (human_bytes, op=schedule, op=schedule_rename, cli schedule-list) and
  de-duplicated two rules that existed in two places (container matching, derived-field list).
###2026.09.11 (catch-up fix)
- Fix: a schedule that had never run looked infinitely overdue to the array-start catch-up logic,
  so it fired immediately on every reboot regardless of its actual scheduled time. Schedules now
  track a creation timestamp and are only caught up relative to that.
###2026.09.11 (later)
- Fix: an orphaned `docker stop` from a killed run kept the schedule lock held, silently skipping
  the next scheduled run. Fix: a single missing source dataset no longer fails the whole schedule -
  it is skipped with a warning and the remaining datasets are still snapshotted.
- Backup target fields are a ROOT now: every source lands at &lt;root&gt;/&lt;basename&gt;. Four call sites
  that open-coded the old rule were corrected (important-flag targeting, prune preview, remote
  snapshot browsing, connection test).
###2026.09.11
- QC pass: 76-check regression suite (test/run.sh); fixes: name collision check across the
  whole tree, orphaned child snapshots swept by recursive prune, own-schedule targets skipped on
  manual runs too, important-flag sync also when nothing needs sending, forged ids rejected,
  list fields (datasets/exclude_props) no longer merged with defaults, PATH appended not prepended.
- Important flag (shive:important) on snapshots, propagated to every copy and reconciled on send;
  manual snapshot deletion; hourly GFS tier; schedules keyed by id with free-form names;
  cron fallback + warning when update_cron cannot see the plugin directory.
###2026.09.08
- Initial release: generic ZFS snapshot scheduling, GFS/age retention per location,
  optional Docker quiesce/resume, local + SSH replication (-I incremental, bookmark base),
  snapshot browser/restore, dashboard tile, Unraid notifications.
</CHANGES>

<!-- ================================================================== -->
<!-- pre-install: sanity checks                                          -->
<!-- ================================================================== -->
<FILE Run="/bin/bash">
<INLINE>
set -e
for bin in zfs zpool jq docker php rsync flock findmnt; do
  command -v "$bin" >/dev/null 2>&amp;1 || { echo "shive: required binary '$bin' not found"; exit 1; }
done
mkdir -p &plgPath;/schedules &plgPath;/state
[ -f &plgPath;/shive.cfg ] || cat > &plgPath;/shive.cfg &lt;&lt;'CFG'
LOG_DIR="/var/log/shive"
NOTIFY_ON_SUCCESS="yes"
DOCKER_STOP_TIMEOUT="60"
SSH_KEY=""
SSH_OPTS="-o BatchMode=yes -o ConnectTimeout=10 -o StrictHostKeyChecking=accept-new"
CATCHUP_ON_START="yes"
RESTORE_CLONE_TTL="7200"
PRERESTORE_KEEP="3"
CFG
[ -f &plgPath;/mappings.json ] || echo '{}' > &plgPath;/mappings.json
</INLINE>
</FILE>

<!-- ================================================================== -->
<!-- package download + install                                          -->
<!-- ================================================================== -->
<FILE Name="&plgPath;/&pkgName;" Run="upgradepkg --install-new">
<URL>&pkgURL;/&pkgName;</URL>
<MD5>&pkgMD5;</MD5>
</FILE>

<!-- ================================================================== -->
<!-- post-install: permissions, cron, recovery, status                   -->
<!-- ================================================================== -->
<FILE Run="/bin/bash">
<INLINE>
set -e
chmod 0755 &emhttp;/scripts/shive-* &emhttp;/event/*
mkdir -p /var/local/shive/{state,locks,restore} /var/log/shive
# regenerate cron from schedules (idempotent) and run container-resume safety net
php &emhttp;/include/cli.php cron-write
&emhttp;/scripts/shive-recover || true
php &emhttp;/include/cli.php status-rebuild || true
echo ""
echo "-----------------------------------------------------------"
echo " shive &version; installed. Settings -> Shive"
echo "-----------------------------------------------------------"
</INLINE>
</FILE>

<!-- ================================================================== -->
<!-- remove                                                              -->
<!-- ================================================================== -->
<FILE Run="/bin/bash" Method="remove">
<INLINE>
# stop running jobs gracefully
pkill -TERM -f "&emhttp;/scripts/shive-run" 2>/dev/null || true
sleep 2
# resume anything left quiesced
&emhttp;/scripts/shive-recover || true
rm -f &plgPath;/shive.cron /boot/config/plugins/dynamix/shive.cron
update_cron
removepkg &name; 2>/dev/null || true
rm -rf &emhttp; /var/local/shive
# NOTE: &plgPath; (schedules, mappings, last-status) is intentionally kept.
echo "shive removed. Config left in &plgPath; - delete manually if unwanted."
</INLINE>
</FILE>

</PLUGIN>
